Before output (2,482 bytes):

```js
var Je=qe();return[Je,Je,…
```

After output (2,457 bytes):

```js
var $=qe();return[$,$,…
```

`hot` goes from `Je` to `$`. The displaced `c53` takes the two-character name instead, which it prints only 3 times against `hot`'s 14. `--twice` reports the output as idempotent.

