Follow-up to #112 (the "related, smaller" part).

The Tracearr and media server (Plex/Jellyfin/Emby) history syncs only fetched plays newer than the newest cached one. Two kinds of play were never picked up unless the cache was emptied:
- older plays, after `watch_history_lookback_days` is raised;
- plays that reach the provider late with older timestamps, e.g. Tautulli history imported into Tracearr.

**Change:** a small planner (`historySyncPlan.ts`) decides between an incremental and a full sync. It runs a full sync over the lookback window when:
- the cache is empty;
- no full sync has been recorded (so existing installs get one after upgrading, which backfills anything already missed);
- the lookback is now longer than the last full sync covered;
- the last full sync is a week old.

Otherwise the sync stays incremental, as before. Rows are deduped by session id, so a repeat full sync only adds what was missing. The last full sync's time and lookback are stored in two internal settings (`history_cache_full_sync_at`, `history_cache_full_sync_days`), and are only written after a sync that finished without error.

**Tested:** `npx vitest run` (416 passed, including new planner tests) and `tsc --noEmit`. Not yet run against a live Tracearr or Plex server.
